reply:
Only the 23.167–168 verses touch on kinship.

23.167: "kroṣṭos tu śṛṇu ... vaṃśam ... yador vaṃśadharasya" says Kroṣṭu is the one who carries Yadu's line, which I read as Kroṣṭu being a descendant of Yadu. The text does not say "son", so I use descendant_of and flag it as uncertain.

23.168: "yasyānvavāyajo viṣṇur harir vṛṣṇikulaprabhuḥ" says Viṣṇu (Hari), lord of the Vṛṣṇi clan, was born in the lineage of the person "yasya" refers to. That person is Kroṣṭu, so Viṣṇu is a descendant of Kroṣṭu. The pronoun's referent is a little unclear, so I flag it too.

